<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "SCORM 2004 4th Edition — Run-Time Environment data model (cmi, adl.nav, adl.data)"@en ;
    dct:description "An OWL 2 DL ontology and SHACL shapes for the run-time data model of SCORM 2004 4th Edition: the cmi data model a SCO reads and writes through API_1484_11 — status, score, time, location, suspend data, learner preferences, comments, interactions and objectives — with each element's data type, access and vocabulary, and ADL's navigation (adl.nav, including the 4th Edition's jump request) and shared data (adl.data) data models. The shapes check the vocabularies, the ranges of scores and measures, SCORM's time formats and the suspend data limit; a CMI snapshot is checked against them at /ns/scorm-rte/validate."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by ADL or IEEE. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Element names in dotted notation (cmi.completion_status, adl.nav.request) are each property's skos:notation; n and m stand for the index of an entry in a collection."@en ,
        "SPM is a smallest permitted maximum: the length every LMS must accept. A longer value is allowed, but only an LMS that supports more keeps it whole, so the shapes report one beyond its SPM as a sh:Warning, not a sh:Violation."@en ,
        "The shapes select nodes by class (sh:targetClass): an RDF producer types the nodes it describes with this ontology's classes. A parsed instance as JSON is checked against the same shapes at POST /ns/scorm-rte/validate, which routes it by its declared type; every result cites its shape."@en ,
        "An instance written as JSON is read into this ontology through the JSON-LD 1.1 context published at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte/context/2026.10.0, which is generated from this document. The shapes at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte/shapes/2026.10.0 constrain that reading, and the Foxxi validator (POST https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte/validate) checks the JSON against the same shapes."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/scorm-rte#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
    dct:creator "Mark Spivey" ;
    dct:contributor "Claude (Anthropic)" ;
    dct:publisher "Foxxi Mediums Inc." ;
    dct:license <https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT> ;
    dct:rights "© 2026 Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Released under the MIT License."@en ;
    dct:created "2026-06-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-12"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2026-10-12"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:language <http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-1/en> ;
    bibo:status <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/status/published> ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Spivey, M. (2026). SCORM 2004 4th Edition — Run-Time Environment data model (cmi, adl.nav, adl.data) (Version 2026.10.0) [Ontology]. Foxxi Mediums Inc. https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte/2026.10.0" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "foxxi-scorm-rte" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-rte#" ;
